1583142236,"weather":0.04653740890761381,"just":0.014926729339563452,"open":0.02802447609715275,"app":0.041142885040734004}},{"id":"doc_1787410476973_ci9nwq_c1","text":"[16:00–21:20] Create · Once · Next - [≈17:57] Once you're here, click API keys, then create new secret key. - [≈18:50] For most models, each request costs under a penny, unless you're using like a deep research or something with long responses. - [≈20:00] Now, because we set the memory context window to five, the agent remembers the past five messages in here. - [≈20:14] If I removed the memory, it would forget after each message, like starting over every time, and there's not much to talk about yet since the agent isn't built out, but once it is, you can ask it to do things, get info, or even just explore what it's capable o… QUOTE: \"Now, because we set the memory context window to five, the agent remembers the past five messages in here.\" (≈20:00) [21:20–26:40] Air · Quality · Trail - [≈23:13] The only other setting I'll change here is switching the units from metric to imperial so I get temperatures in Fahrenheit. - [≈23:46] Each entry includes the trail name, the mileage, elevation gain, and a rough estimate of how long it'll take, plus how much shade is on the trail. - [≈24:23] That way, I can add more tabs later for hikes, family trails, mountain biking, rock climbing, or anything else. - [≈25:14] So, the message is fully customized based on the trail it picks, the weather, air quality, and everything else going on that day. QUOTE: \"Each entry includes the trail name, the mileage, elevation gain, and a rough estimate of how long it'll take, plus how much shade is on the trail.\" (≈23:46) [26:40–32:00] Prompt · Json · Ask - [≈28:20] Then, real quick, I'll rename the node to something like get air quality and update the description so I remember what it's doing. - [≈29:54] The most important elements to include in your prompt are role, what kind of assistant is it? - [≈30:38] It gave me a clean, well structured prompt that covers everything I need. - [≈31:40] Now, it gives me step-by-step instructions, tells me exactly what to change, and it even includes the text I need to copy and paste. QUOTE: \"Then, real quick, I'll rename the node to something like get air quality and update the description so I remember what it's doing.\" (≈28:20) [32:00–35:22] Save · Futureedia · Workflows - [≈33:33] Now it searches the list and it came back with a few options and it gave me its best choice which would allow a little extra time for stretching or a cool down. - [≈33:54] That was just a really quick demo to show that chat feature, but when you give access to a lot more tools and information, plus the ability to add and change things across your calendar, documents, or anything else, this gets super powerful. - [≈34:34] And at Futureedia, we use agents for all kinds of tasks, and no matter what industry you're in, there's a good chance agents can save you","t0":729,"t1":1457,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"13":0.0425826141028116,"14":0.09184405546074947,"16":0.04469900281680875,"17":0.05533530604819355,"18":0.052745055603281285,"20":0.25260615647762386,"21":0.09457850652344202,"22":0.04592202773037474,"23":0.1703304564112464,"24":0.04469900281680875,"25":0.04728925326172101,"26":0.09184405546074947,"28":0.08330695663163167,"29":0.04728925326172101,"30":0.0425826141028116,"31":0.05533530604819355,"32":0.09767857145579928,"33":0.1582351668098439,"34":0.0893980056336175,"35":0.04469900281680875,"38":0.04728925326172101,"40":0.1223796988242813,"46":0.09767857145579928,"50":0.04469900281680875,"54":0.0893980056336175,"57":0.052745055603281285,"00":0.17773294709959128,"create":0.038646637208916125,"once":0.07804994039685424,"next":0.027239671712517403,"re":0.04614103070269984,"here":0.06152137427026645,"click":0.04359264220639079,"api":0.028040540996045155,"keys":0.03554658941991825,"then":0.047273618374928876,"secret":0.052745055603281285,"key":0.028040540996045155,"most"