mo":0.0425826141028116,"show":0.030839950261008848,"chat":0.02750053663344571,"feature":0.04359264220639079,"give":0.024293787312189244,"access":0.03156568659321834,"lot":0.025561372742870753,"tools":0.024293787312189244,"information":0.02982992215742966,"ability":0.03999236365789934,"across":0.0331693357849928,"calendar":0.04165347831581583,"documents":0.03999236365789934,"gets":0.03665295003033621,"super":0.04165347831581583,"powerful":0.0407932329414271,"agents":0.04940225473696404,"kinds":0.05533530604819355,"tasks":0.030156929710042305,"matter":0.0425826141028116,"industry":0.052745055603281285,"good":0.02698454055335239,"chance":0.05533530604819355}},{"id":"doc_1787410476973_ci9nwq_c2","text":"time and money with research, customer support, sales workflows, financial automations, you name it. - [≈35:02] But if you want to go way more in depth on learning AI on Futureedia, we have over 20 comprehensive courses on how to incorporate AI into your life and career to get ahead and save time. QUOTE: \"But if you want to go way more in depth on learning AI on Futureedia, we have over 20 comprehensive courses on how to incorporate AI into your life and career to get ahead and save time.\" (≈35:02) FRAMEWORKS & RULES: - [≈23:57] These estimated times were calculated using a formula I generated with Chat GPT. TAKEAWAYS & HEURISTICS: - For most people, that's going to feel like completely unlimited usage for 14 days to see if you want to continue. - That means you can build a full-blown agent, one that reasons, remembers, and acts all from a single node connected to whatever services you want. - It might remember previous steps in a conversation or pull from external memory sources like documents or a vector database. - And finally, always set guard rails so your agent doesn't go off the rails and keep updating them as your use case evolves. - I always come back to relating these to a human and how humans structure things within an organization. NOTABLE QUOTES: - [≈3:08] \"It might remember previous steps in a conversation or pull from external memory sources like documents or a vector database.\" - [≈8:28] \"And finally, always set guard rails so your agent doesn't go off the rails and keep updating them as your use case evolves.\" - [≈12:55] \"For most people, that's going to feel like completely unlimited usage for 14 days to see if you want to continue.\" - [≈20:00] \"Now, because we set the memory context window to five, the agent remembers the past five messages in here.\" - [≈23:46] \"Each entry includes the trail name, the mileage, elevation gain, and a rough estimate of how long it'll take, plus how much shade is on the trail.\" - [≈28:20] \"Then, real quick, I'll rename the node to something like get air quality and update the description so I remember what it's doing.\" - [≈35:02] \"But if you want to go way more in depth on learning AI on Futureedia, we have over 20 comprehensive courses on how to incorporate AI into your life and career to get ahead and save time.\" QUESTIONS THIS ANSWERS: - What does the source teach about agent? - What does the source teach about ll? - What does the source teach about like? - What does the source teach about just? - How does first ai agent 25min apply today?","t0":1458,"t1":2121,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"12":0.04475727841992898,"14":0.09868779577794186,"20":0.19387789333042982,"23":0.09151129712614034,"28":0.08951455683985796,"35":0.14408921859993637,"46":0.052478534747578964,"55":0.048029739533312125,"57":0.056675342237009006,"time":0.07824662695801643,"money":0.056675342237009006,"research":0.04141123026038246,"customer":0.046840938696611836,"support":0.04141123026038246,"sales":0.052478534747578964,"workflows":0.04216739923716941,"financial":0.04934389788897093,"automations":0.056675342237009006,"name":0.05745408331593639,"02":0.170026026711027,"want":0.1053985365562928,"go":0.09974724320836383,"way":0.06970513833088349,"depth":0.17837581393368954,"learning":0.137266945689210