chestrates multiple specialized agents (e.g., data retrieval, analysis, execution) to solve complex, real‑world tasks end‑to‑end.  \nIt combines a unified orchestration engine with plug‑in tool integrations, enabling rapid, reliable automation across diverse domains.","uploadedAt":"2026-09-06T04:22:41.685Z","tsMode":"estimate","chunks":[{"id":"doc_1788668561683_grggsf_c0","text":"Q: Explain what SHADDAI is in 2 lines. A: SHADDAI is an AI‑driven, modular platform that orchestrates multiple specialized agents (e.g., data retrieval, analysis, execution) to solve complex, real‑world tasks end‑to‑end. It combines a unified orchestration engine with plug‑in tool integrations, enabling rapid, reliable automation across diverse domains.","t0":0,"t1":19,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"explain":0.12769146912796536,"shaddai":0.4124668083598254,"lines":0.16473806358277499,"ai":0.07036044970172751,"driven":0.18005275916259691,"modular":0.19091870860009075,"platform":0.1355341505286005,"orchestrates":0.2062334041799127,"multiple":0.09501992189115728,"specialized":0.18005275916259691,"agents":0.08037375149327679,"data":0.0688392768738415,"retrieval":0.13855741856545922,"analysis":0.16473806358277499,"execution":0.15387211414528112,"solve":0.14942336800295308,"complex":0.1355341505286005,"real":0.10522897326292703,"world":0.12769146912796536,"tasks":0.0981261113372458,"end":0.15941045262267076,"combines":0.2062334041799127,"unified":0.18005275916259691,"orchestration":0.17162447398925013,"engine":0.2062334041799127,"plug":0.17162447398925013,"tool":0.09123970093077065,"integrations":0.17162447398925013,"enabling":0.2062334041799127,"rapid":0.2062334041799127,"reliable":0.14184389802800723,"automation":0.15891568654522414,"across":0.1079280274058154,"diverse":0.2062334041799127,"domains":0.16473806358277499}}]},{"id":"doc_video_tooling_nexus","name":"video_media_pipeline_tooling","text":"VIDEO AND MEDIA TOOLING PIPELINE - concrete commands for probing, extracting, transcribing, and beat-detecting a video file.\n\nPROBE FIRST: ffprobe -v error -show_format -show_streams -of json returns duration, fps, resolution, codec before anything downstream commits. A wrong assumption here is paid for in every later step.\n\nEXTRACT AUDIO FOR ANALYSIS: ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vn -ac 1 -ar 22050 -c:a pcm_s16le -y output.wav pulls mono at 22050 which matches librosa and beatlyzer defaults so nothing resamples twice. whisper.cpp instead requires 16000 Hz 16-bit PCM WAV: ffmpeg -i in.mp4 -ar 16000 -ac 1 -c:a pcm_s16le out.wav. -vn drops video, -y overwrites without prompting. You cannot hear audio from a file you never opened - ask for the path, then run these.\n\nTRANSCRIPTION: default to faster-whisper on CPU. pip install faster-whisper, no build step, PyAV bundles ffmpeg so MP4 decodes without a system install, int8 small model benchmarks far faster and lighter than openai-whisper. Pass beam_size explicitly because openai-whisper defaults to 1 while faster-whisper defaults to 5, so unpinned comparisons are meaningless. Use word_timestamps=True for per-word timings and vad_filter=True with vad_parameters dict min_silence_duration_ms=500 to drop silence. The segments result is a generator, nothing runs until you iterate it, so call list(segments) to force completion. Reach for whisper.cpp only for a standalone exe, lowest RAM, -owts word-timing export, --print-colors per-word confidence, or VAD tuning with --vad --vad-threshold 0.5. Reach for openai-whisper only for --task translate into English. None of them detect beats.\n\nFRAME EXTRACTION: for a known target count use video-to-keyframes cli-script.py input.mp4 output/ --enable-keyframes --target-frames 12 --inference-tolerance 0.00001 which estimates the SSIM threshold needed to land near N frames. For unknown counts with varying motion use the DIS optical flow Python frame extractor with motion_score_px and in_bounds_ratio thresholds and a selection_reason column per keyframe. decord is random access not selection: VideoReader(path, ctx=cpu(0)) then vr.get_batch([1,3,5,7,9]). Codec motion vectors via ffmpeg -flags2 +export_mvs -debug vis_mv=pf+bf give bitstream motion cheaper than pixel flow when present.\n\nBEAT AND BPM: extract audio to wav first, then choose by output type. For a human-readable report with a four-panel PNG sharing one time axis - waveform, event markers, brightness, spectrogram - use beatlyzer song.wav --format json --print-json --quiet which yields tempo_bpm, events with strength_0_1, sections, and energy_profile, plus schema beatlyzer.analysis/v1 and an ai_notes block declaring units. For arrays to reshape into cut points use librosa: build ONE onset envelope with librosa.onset.onset_strength(y, sr, aggregate=np.median) then feed it to librosa.feature.tempo and librosa.beat.beat_track, never recompute per function. Keep units as seconds with units=time instead of hand-converting frames, use backtrack=True when onsets mark cuts, start_bpm to lock a known tempo, trim=False when the track starts quietly. Do not run both as a second opinion - beatlyzer is librosa underneath - run beatlyzer first for semantics, librosa second on the same wav for numbers. Derive downbeats as beat_times[i % 4] for 4/4 and mark the assumption.\n\nCUT POINTS: cut_frames = sorted(set(round(t * fps) for t in beat_times)).\n\nINTER-AGENT OUTPUT CONTRACT: anything passing between agents carries a versioned schema string, explicit units, and stated assumptions in the payload. That is what makes an output safe to hand to another agent without a human re-reading documentation first.\n\nCOMPOSITE PIPELINE: probe with ffprobe, plan with scene/motion/blur/exposure analysis or a contact sheet, extract frames by count or motion, burn timestamps, extract audio to mono wav at 22050, run beatlyzer then librosa for beats, run faster-whisper with word timestamps for speech. Full reference with per-tool routing tables in shaddai-design-studio tools/VIDEO.md.","uploadedAt":1791306775446,"chunks":[],"kind":"knowledge","tsMode":"none"}]